D;
hello.a well-formed request line is split into its three parts;
hello.parse,hello.get_root,hello.Parsed;
D;
hello.a head is incomplete until CRLF CRLF, whatever has arrived so far;
hello.head_end,hello.get_root,hello.parse,hello.Parsed;
D;
hello.a head ends at the first blank line and not at a later one;
hello.head_end,hello.parse,hello.Parsed;
D;
hello.every way of malforming a request line names itself;
hello.reason;
D;
hello.a target that is not UTF-8 is refused rather than decoded;
hello.reason,hello.parse,hello.Parsed;
D;
hello.an empty head and a head of blank lines are both refused;
hello.parse,hello.Parsed,hello.reason;
D;
hello.a request with a body is answered from its head alone;
hello.head_end,hello.reason;
D;
hello.a response declares the byte length of its body, not its character count;
hello.response;
D;
hello.a good head answers 200 and every bad one answers 400;
hello.answer,hello.get_root,hello.ok,hello.bad;
D;
hello.the simulated socket answers a well-formed request with the fixed 200;
hello.get_root,hello.listen_and_serve,std.net.net,hello.later_chunks,hello.first_chunk,hello.ok;
D;
hello.a request split across packets is read to its terminator;
hello.serve_one,std.net.net,hello.later_chunks,hello.first_chunk,hello.ok;
D;
hello.a malformed request is answered 400 and the connection is closed;
hello.serve_one,std.net.net,hello.later_chunks,hello.first_chunk,hello.bad;
D;
hello.a peer that says nothing gets a 400 rather than a hung thread;
hello.serve_one,std.net.net,hello.later_chunks,hello.first_chunk,hello.bad;
D;
hello.a head that never ends stops after `max_chunks` and answers 400;
hello.serve_one,std.net.net,hello.max_chunks,hello.bad;
D;
hello.each accepted connection is answered exactly once;
hello.listen_and_serve,std.net.net,hello.get_root,hello.ok;
D;
